    "created_at": "2023-06-29T20:57:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-06-29T20:57:58Z",
    "body": "@reillyeon I know this is an old, closed issue. But I discovered what I think may be a flaw with relying on the `readable` `writable` attributes: they seem to still be `null` even if you have a serial connection open with this same port in another tab 😅 \r\n\r\nIt seems like the only solution then is to try to open it and looks for the failed to open because already open error.",
